# For more info on HTTP files go to https://aka.ms/vs/httpfile
### Variables
@apiUrl = https://localhost:5001
@adminToken = 
@userToken = 

### 1. Login as Admin
# @name adminLogin
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### Store admin token from the previous response
# @name setAdminToken
# In a real environment, extract this from the response above
# For manual testing, copy the token and paste it here
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body}}

### 2. Login as User
# @name userLogin
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "password": "user123"
}

### Store user token from the previous response
# @name setUserToken
@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body}}

### 3. Test v1 Endpoints

### 3.1 Get All Contacts (v1, User access)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3.2 Get Contact by ID (v1, User access)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/v1/contacts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3.3 Create Contact (v1, Admin access)
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "phone": "555-1234",
  "address": "123 Main St",
  "city": "Anytown",
  "state": "CA",
  "zipCode": "12345"
}

### 3.4 Update Contact (v1, Admin access)
PUT {{apiUrl}}/api/v1/contacts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "John Doe Updated",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "phone": "555-1234",
  "address": "123 Main St",
  "city": "Anytown",
  "state": "CA",
  "zipCode": "12345"
}

### 3.5 Delete Contact (v1, Admin access)
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/api/v1/contacts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Test v2 Endpoints

### 4.1 Get Contacts Summary (v2, User access)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/v2/contacts/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 4.2 Get All Contacts (v2, User access)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/v2/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 4.3 Get Contact by ID (v2, User access)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/v2/contacts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 4.4 Create Contact (v2, Admin access)
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/v2/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Smith",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "phone": "555-5678",
  "address": "456 Oak Ave",
  "city": "Somewhere",
  "state": "NY",
  "zipCode": "67890"
}

### 5. Test Authorization Failures

### 5.1 Try to create contact with User token (should fail)
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/v2/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Will Fail",
  "email": "fail@example.com",
  "phone": "555-9999"
}

### 5.2 Try to access endpoint without token (should fail)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/v2/contacts